Imagine you build a Node.js application on your Mac.

Your application needs:

Node.js 22
npm
PostgreSQL
Redis
Kafka

Environment variables
System libraries
Specific npm package versions

Everything works perfectly on your machine.

Then you give the project to another developer.

They install:

Node.js 20
PostgreSQL 16
different Redis version
They run:

npm install
npm run dev

And suddenly:

❌ Application doesn't work
❌ Dependency error
❌ Database connection error
❌ Node version mismatch

Then they tell you:
"Bro, your project isn't working."

And you say:
"It works on my machine!" 😄

This is one of the major problems Docker helps solve.